# Arbitrary-precision floating point. There is no binary arbitrary-precision float that is exact and portable, and the
# value most code reaching for a "big float" actually wants is exact base-10: prices, sums of fractions, anything where
# 0.1 + 0.2 must equal 0.3. That is the `decimal` module (an unbounded big-integer mantissa with a scale), so big-float
# IS big-decimal -- this module is the named entry point that builds one from text or from a platform float.

load @term/base/code/decimal
  find big-decimal
  find make-big-decimal

# an arbitrary-precision (exact base-10) float from its text, e.g. "3.14159265358979323846"
task make-big-float
  take value, like text
  like big-decimal
  send back
    call make-big-decimal
      read value
